#: ../../../specs/globaldisco-v3.rst:4
msgid "Global Discovery v3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/globaldisco-v3.rst:7
msgid "Announcements"
msgstr "公告"

#: ../../../specs/globaldisco-v3.rst:9
msgid ""
"A device should announce itself at startup. It does this by an HTTPS POST to "
"the announce server URL. Standard discovery currently requires the path to "
"be \"/v2/\", yet this can be up to the discovery server. The POST has a JSON "
"payload listing connection addresses (if any)::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/globaldisco-v3.rst:14
msgid ""
"{\n"
"        addresses: [\"tcp://192.0.2.45:22000\", \"tcp://:22202\", "
"\"relay://192.0.2.99:22028\"],\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/globaldisco-v3.rst:18
msgid ""
"It's OK for the \"addresses\" field to be either the empty list (``[]``), "
"``null``, or missing entirely. An announcement with the field missing or "
"empty is however not useful..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/globaldisco-v3.rst:22
msgid ""
"Any empty or unspecified IP addresses (i.e. addresses like ``tcp://:22000``, "
"``tcp://0.0.0.0:22000``, ``tcp://[::]:22000``) are interpreted as referring "
"to the source IP address of the announcement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/globaldisco-v3.rst:26
msgid ""
"The device ID of the announcing device is not part of the announcement. "
"Instead, the server requires that the client perform certificate "
"authentication. The device ID is deduced from the presented certificate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/globaldisco-v3.rst:30
msgid ""
"The server response is empty, with code ``204`` (No Content) on success. If "
"no certificate was presented, status ``403`` (Forbidden) is returned. If the "
"posted data doesn't conform to the expected format, ``400`` (Bad Request) is "
"returned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/globaldisco-v3.rst:35
msgid ""
"In successful responses, the server may return a ``Reannounce-After`` header "
"containing the number of seconds after which the client should perform a new "
"announcement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/globaldisco-v3.rst:39
msgid ""
"In error responses, the server may return a ``Retry-After`` header "
"containing the number of seconds after which the client should retry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/globaldisco-v3.rst:42
msgid ""
"Performing announcements significantly more often than indicated by the "
"``Reannounce-After`` or ``Retry-After`` headers may result in the client "
"being throttled. In such cases the server may respond with status code "
"``429`` (Too Many Requests)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/globaldisco-v3.rst:48
msgid "Queries"
msgstr "查詢"

#: ../../../specs/globaldisco-v3.rst:50
msgid ""
"Queries are performed as HTTPS GET requests to the announce server URL. The "
"requested device ID is passed as the query parameter \"device\", in "
"canonical string form, i.e. ``https://discovery.syncthing.net/?"
"device=ABC12345-....``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/globaldisco-v3.rst:54
msgid ""
"Successful responses will have status code ``200`` (OK) and carry a JSON "
"payload of the same format as the announcement above. The response will not "
"contain empty or unspecified addresses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/globaldisco-v3.rst:58
msgid ""
"If the \"device\" query parameter is missing or malformed, the status code "
"400 (Bad Request) is returned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/globaldisco-v3.rst:61
msgid ""
"If the device ID is of a valid format but not found in the registry, 404 "
"(Not Found) is returned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/globaldisco-v3.rst:64
msgid ""
"If the client has exceeded a rate limit, the server may respond with 429 "
"(Too Many Requests)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/globaldisco-v3.rst:68
msgid "Authentication"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/globaldisco-v3.rst:70
msgid ""
"Global discovery is spoken over HTTPS and is protected against attackers in "
"the same manner as other HTTPS traffic. However, there are a few Syncthing "
"specific considerations on top of this. As mentioned above, for "
"announcements the client must provide a certificate to prove ownership of "
"the announced device ID."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/globaldisco-v3.rst:76
msgid ""
"In addition, Syncthing has a mechanism to verify the identity of the "
"discovery server.  While this would normally be accomplished by using a CA "
"signed certificate, Syncthing often runs in environments with outdated or "
"simply nonexistent root CA bundles. Instead, Syncthing can verify the "
"discovery server certificate fingerprint using the device ID mechanism. This "
"is certificate pinning and conveyed in the Syncthing configuration as a "
"synthetic \"id\" parameter on the discovery server URL: ``https://discovery."
"syncthing.net/?id=...``. The \"id\" parameter is not, in fact, sent to the "
"discovery server - it's used by Syncthing itself to know which certificate "
"to expect on the server side."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/globaldisco-v3.rst:87
msgid ""
"The public discovery network uses this authentication mechanism instead of "
"CA signed certificates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../specs/globaldisco-v3.rst:90
msgid ""
"The discovery server prints its certificate ID in this manner on startup."
msgstr ""
